{"id": "15fa314f-1fe8-4910-9565-57d1c4727809", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"id": "tooluse_KFzRff4I8SziQo1wltL1Cn", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "ebs-review-core", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["storage-ebs-expertise", "exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only pre-launch Amazon EBS review (Review mode of the storage-ebs-expertise skill; read it with skill_read and its references/review-operational.md, data-collection.md, finding-logic.md, review-report-format.md). Cover these areas ONLY: (1) Capacity and quota headroom, (2) Observability, (3) Cost hygiene, (4) Encryption posture, (5) Deletion protection. Another agent covers Resilience (DLM/AWS Backup/Recycle Bin) so skip those.",
  "context": "Customer launches next week and asks 'Is my storage production-ready?'. Account 012345678901_1, Region us-east-1 only. Never run mutating calls. Do not assume which volumes are critical - list volumes with attachments/tags/instance names so the operator can say, and note criticality is unconfirmed. Do not invent IDs or numbers; every number must come from an API call you made, with units (throughput in MiB/s) and time window.",
  "resources": ["EC2 volumes, snapshots, instances in us-east-1", "Service Quotas service code ebs", "CloudWatch alarms in AWS/EBS and AWS/EC2 namespaces", "KMS keys used by volumes"],
  "timeframe": "Metrics: last 14 days up to 2026-11-11T19:13:00Z",
  "criteria": "Return findings per area with Severity (High/Medium/Low/Indeterminate), Resource ID, Evidence, Fix (proposal only), plus: volume inventory summary (count by type/state/encrypted, sizes, IOPS/throughput provisioned), per-instance check that summed attached-volume IOPS/MiB/s provisioned vs the instance EBS baseline (DescribeInstanceTypes, convert MB/s to MiB/s) and measured peak usage, quota usage vs applied value (flag >=80%), pending quota requests, gp2 volumes (gp3 candidates), unattached volumes, alarm coverage on in-use volumes, encryption-by-default + default KMS key + KMS key state, unencrypted volumes/snapshots, public snapshots + snapshot block public access state, DeleteOnTermination on each non-root attached volume (and root), snapshot lock. List every API that failed or was gated under 'Not checked'. Be concise: tables, no raw dumps."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review EBS capacity, alarms, cost, encryption, deletion protection"}, {"id": "tooluse_Zt9NvBF1pR2CXiRWffr6G9", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "ebs-review-resilience", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["storage-ebs-expertise"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Read-only Resilience review of Amazon EBS (Resilience and the Recycle Bin part of Deletion protection in references/review-operational.md of the storage-ebs-expertise skill; read it with skill_read and read_skill_resource, plus data-collection.md and finding-logic.md).",
  "context": "Customer launches next week and asks 'Is my storage production-ready?'. Account 012345678901_1, Region us-east-1. Never run mutating calls. Do not assume which volumes are critical or the RPO; list volumes with attachments/tags/instance names and say criticality and RPO are unconfirmed. Do not invent IDs or numbers.",
  "resources": ["EC2 volumes (including root volumes) in us-east-1", "Amazon Data Lifecycle Manager policies", "AWS Backup plans, selections, protected resources, recovery points", "Recycle Bin rules for EBS snapshots and AMIs", "DescribeLockedSnapshots"],
  "timeframe": "Now (2026-11-11T19:13:00Z); check latest backup age vs schedule",
  "criteria": "For each volume: is it matched by an ENABLED DLM policy (case-sensitive target tags) or an AWS Backup selection (by ARN, tag condition, or resource type)? Latest recovery point/snapshot age vs schedule (use ListRecoveryPointsByResource with ManagedByAWSBackupOnly=true, and latest aws:dlm:* tagged snapshot). Cross-Region copy for DR (DLM copy actions or Backup copy rules). Recycle Bin rules and locked snapshots. Return findings with Severity (High/Medium/Low/Indeterminate), Resource ID, Evidence, Fix (proposal only). If a read call is gated behind approval or denied, list it under 'Not checked' and state which conclusion remains unconfirmed; do not try to bypass. Be concise: tables, no raw dumps."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Review EBS backup coverage and snapshot protection"}], "created_at": null}

{"id": "60fab3ac-47a9-4ea9-9a8d-7d4242e3df94", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The Trial plan's selections come back empty, so it doesn't actually protect anything despite having copy/rule details configured. I should check the EFS selection using GetBackupSelection since that's allowlisted, and also look at recovery points to confirm nothing is backed up under this plan.

I notice the snapshots at 16:50, 17:41, and 18:49 are spaced irregularly for a supposedly hourly schedule with retention of 2 — worth flagging since I can't inspect the actual policy. I still need instance names from DescribeInstances to make the report readable.

"}], "parent_id": "76aea8c5-d9e3-467c-b2a3-685cb412e4a1"}

